# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the zim extension's parallel-scan test.
#
# libzim is linked WITHOUT tsan instrumentation, so tsan cannot see the mutexes
# that already guard libzim's own internal caches, and false-reports data races
# on their internal allocations under concurrent reads. Verified thread-safe in
# libzim 9.7.0 source:
#   - DirectDirentAccessor::getDirent locks m_direntCacheLock around its LRU
#     dirent cache (src/dirent_accessor.cpp).
#   - Cluster blob data / FileImpl use libzim's ConcurrentCache (mutex-guarded).
#
# These suppress races whose racy frame is INSIDE libzim (zim::*). A race in this
# extension's own code (duckdb::zim_ext::*) is NOT matched and will still fail the
# test -- which is the point of running it.
race:zim::DirectDirentAccessor
race:zim::Cluster
race:zim::FileImpl
race:zim::Reader
race:zim::DirentReader
